## Output
Respond with a single JSON object (no markdown fences, no preamble) with exactly two fields:

- `updated_memory`: the updated rolling memory, as plain text (same rules as before — keep it compact and factual; preserve superseded facts only through their current replacement, for example "Limit changed from 4K to 20K" when the change itself matters; never retain an obsolete fact as current; if nothing worth remembering was added, return the current memory unchanged, or a brief empty-safe note if there was no prior memory and nothing important).
- `fact_candidates`: a (possibly empty) array of separately-protected critical facts found in the newly expired turn above. Each candidate must have: `fact_slot_id` (reuse an existing slot id above when this is about the same topic, otherwise a short new stable id), `category` (one of: fact, decision, requirement, preference, open_task, correction, cancellation), `content` (a short, self-contained statement of the fact), `speaker` (`user` or `assistant` — whoever is actually asserting this as true, not whoever it's about), `source_span` (an exact, verbatim quote copied from the user question or final verdict text above — never paraphrased, never invented), and `grounding` (`explicit_user_statement` if the user stated it directly, or `explicit_confirmed_decision` only if the user explicitly confirmed/agreed to something — never for a suggestion the user has not yet confirmed).

Only include a fact_candidate when it is an explicit, concrete statement — never a hypothetical, a quoted/reported third-party claim, a hedge ("maybe", "might", "could", "what if"), or an assistant suggestion the user has not confirmed. Use category `cancellation` when the user explicitly removes a requirement with no replacement value (content should state that nothing is currently required, e.g. "No current limit — explicitly removed"). When in doubt, omit the candidate — `fact_candidates` is allowed, and expected, to be empty most of the time. Never include a candidate whose `source_span` is not an exact substring of the user question or final verdict text above.
